# Engineering Standards

Build every module to enterprise / industry-standard quality. Match this
codebase's existing patterns — do not introduce foreign ones.

## Next.js (read first — see AGENTS.md)

This is Next.js 16 with breaking changes. BEFORE writing any Next.js code
(route handlers, `page.tsx`/`layout.tsx`, server actions, data fetching,
caching, metadata, edge logic), read the relevant guide under
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/`. Heed runtime deprecation notices —
e.g. use the `proxy` convention, not the deprecated `middleware`.
(Search tools skip `node_modules`; open these docs with the file reader.)

## Layered structure

- `src/app/(dashboard)/<module>/` — route + page UI
- `src/app/api/<module>/route.ts` — server endpoints
- `src/lib/<module>/` — domain logic, pure & React-free (unit-testable)
- `src/components/<module>/` — UI components
- `src/hooks/`, `src/types/` — shared hooks and types
- `supabase/migrations/NNN_*.sql` — sequentially numbered schema changes

## Data & security (non-negotiable)

- Every new table: enable RLS with account-scoped policies (follow the
  `017_account_sharing` model). No table ships without policies.
- Migrations are idempotent: `IF NOT EXISTS`, `DROP POLICY IF EXISTS`.
- Authorize and validate every mutation server-side (use existing
  `roles` / `api-context` helpers). Never expose the service-role key
  to the client.

## UI conventions (non-negotiable)

- **Data tables** must ship with **search, filters, and pagination**
  (see `src/app/(dashboard)/tables/page.tsx` and the Contacts page).
  Small/account-scoped sets may filter+paginate client-side; large
  sets paginate server-side via range queries.
- **Destructive / irreversible actions** (delete, archive, revoke,
  transfer) must confirm via the shared `ConfirmDialog`
  (`@/components/ui/confirm-dialog`) — never `window.confirm`.
- Page roots use `space-y-*` only — NO page-level padding. The
  dashboard layout (`dashboard-shell.tsx`) already applies
  `p-4 sm:p-6`; adding `p-6` on the page double-pads.
- Reuse `src/components/ui/*` primitives; gate role-restricted
  actions with `useCan(...)` / `GatedButton`.

## Type safety & testing

- Strict TypeScript; no `any` in domain code. Shared types in `src/types`.
- Domain logic in `src/lib` ships with colocated `*.test.ts` (Vitest).

## Quality gates (must pass before "done")

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run test
npm run format:check
```

## Workflow per module

1. Short design note (data model, RLS, API surface, UI) → confirm.
2. Migration + RLS → `lib` logic + tests → API routes → UI → sidebar wiring.
3. Run quality gates, then summarize.
